--[[
  Equadis' Classic Overhaul :: OctoWow item names

  Every item the server's own database lists, by id: the name the server uses
  and its quality. Generated from https://octowow.st/db/ (AoWoW) on 2026-09-13.

  Why this exists. The loot snapshot beside it (pfquest_loot.lua) is a
  reverse-loot table: it knows an item only if some Turtle mob or object drops
  it. That is 7,666 names. It does not know a single OctoWow-custom item, nor
  anything that is not a drop -- Hearthstone, quest rewards, vendor goods,
  crafted items -- so the browser's search had nothing to find for most of
  what a player types. This is the name index the search was missing.

  How it was gathered. The site caps every listing at 500 rows, so each item
  class was pulled in item-level bands, splitting any band that hit the cap.
  Two limits remain and are worth knowing about:

    * The site's "OctoWow Items" category ignores every filter, so it could
      not be sliced. Its items were reached through their real classes
      instead, which the level filter does honour.
    * Items at item level 0 or 1 with no required level -- most quest items,
      much junk, some consumables -- exceed the cap in three classes and no
      filter on the site can divide them. The first 500 of each are here; the
      loot snapshot's names fill in 2076 more that are drops; NPC-given quest
      items past that point are not. A name search that finds nothing for a
      low-level quest item is this gap, not a typo.

  quality: 0 poor, 1 common, 2 uncommon, 3 rare, 4 epic, 5 legendary,
  6 artifact; absent for the loot-snapshot fill-ins, which carry no quality.
  Read through itemdatabase:OctoItemDB(). Do not edit by hand -- regenerate.
]]--

